  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marsabit Rapid Drought Emergency Response and Livelihood Protection Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Marsabit Rapid Drought Emergency Response and Livelihood Protection Project is a short-term, life-saving intervention designed to mitigate the worsening impacts of the ongoing drought on highly vulnerable pastoralist in North Horr, and Laisamis sub-counties of Marsabit County. Informed by the 2025 Short Rains Food and Nutrition Security Assessment (KFSSG, January 2026), the project responds to deteriorating food security and sexual and gender-based violence. With a total budget of GBP 25,000, the project prioritizes immediate actions that protect lives and livelihoods while preventing further erosion of household coping capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
